 "indicator": {
  "definition": {
   "definition": "Rupee securities held by the Reserve Bank are its holdings of Government of India dated securities and treasury bills, reported as item 3 'Rupee Securities (including Treasury Bills)' in the WSS 'RBI — Liabilities and Assets' table. They rise when the RBI absorbs government paper (through primary-market devolvement, outright open-market operations, or its liquidity operations) and fall when it sells securities back. Growth in this line therefore shows the central bank financing or absorbing government borrowing, which matters for both liquidity conditions and the fiscal-monetary interface.",
